[208.507622, "o", "  ⚙ bash coqchk -silent -o plus_comm.vo; echo \"COQCHK_EXIT=$?\"\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-flash-next — 6 tool call(s) so far\r\n  │ Let me confirm the fresh timestamp against the source and that no artifac…\r\n[approval] bash: ls -l --time-style=full-iso plus_comm.v plus_comm.vo plus_comm.vos plus_comm.vok plus_comm.glob .plus_comm.aux — approved\r\n  ⚙ bash ls -l --time-style=full-iso plus_comm.v plus_comm.vo plus_comm.vos plu…\r\n    ✓ bash — exit 0\r\n  qwen3.8-flash-next — 7 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ task \r\n    ✓ task implementor — 7 tool call(s)\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 11 tool call(s) so far\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\n  ⚙ note \r\n    ✓ note — Coq 8.18.0 is installed (/usr/bin/coqc, coqtop, coqchk). Bui\r\n  [tools] 12 call(s) without changing a file — nudging to decide\r\n  deepseek-v4.1-flash — 12 tool call(s) so far\r\nThe work is done and verified on disk. Summary:\r\n\r\n**What changed** — `plus_comm.v` no longer contains `admit`. The two holes were filled and two helper lemmas added, since the inductive step needs `n + S m = S (n + m)`:\r\n\r\n- `plus_comm_n_O : forall n, n + 0 = n` — induction on `n`.\r\n- `plus_comm_n_Sm : forall n m, n + S m = S (n + m)` — induction on `n`.\r\n- `plus_comm` — induction on `n`; base case rewrites with `plus_comm_n_O`, step rewrites with the IH then `plus_comm_n_Sm`.\r\n\r\nEach case uses `change` to state the goal shape explicitly rather than relying on `simpl`, because Coq ≥ 8.12 defines `Nat.add` by recursion on the *second* argument — `simpl` would not reduce the step case the way the original `admit` comments assumed.\r\n\r\n**The check that shows it works** — artifacts were deleted first, so the `.vo` is provably a product of the current source, not a leftover:\r\n\r\n- `coqc plus_comm.v` → exit 0, `plus_comm.vo` (15030 bytes) written.\r\n- `Check plus_comm` → `forall n m : nat, n + m = m + n`.\r\n- `Print Assumptions plus_comm` → `Closed under the global context` (same for both lemmas).\r\n- `coqchk -silent -o plus_comm.vo` → exit 0, `Axioms: <none>` — an independent kernel-level confirmation.\r\n- `grep -E 'admit|Admitted|Axiom|Parameter'` → no matches.\r\n\r\nTwo things worth flagging:\r\n\r\n- I could not write `plus_comm.v` myself — this role's write scope is `docs/**`, `specs/**`, `*.md`. The edit was made by delegating to the `implementor` role, and I read the resulting file back to confirm the contents before accepting it.\r\n- The `verifier` role's shell is allowlisted and cannot run `coqc`, `coqtop`, or `rm`, so it could not perform the rebuild checks; those were routed to `implementor`. Build artifacts (`plus_comm.vo`, `.glob`, `.aux`, `.vok`, `.vos`) exist in the working tree and are not covered by `.gitignore`, so they will show as untracked files — say the word if you want them ignored or removed.\r\n\r\n[refusal] role=coordinator model=deepseek-v4.1-flash tools=12 surface=016d83f6af9a\r\n"]
